  "caveats": [
    "Five repeated blocks use one synthetic separable JavaScript workload; checks are clustered within run.",
    "Intervals are descriptive small-sample t intervals, not broad task-population inference.",
    "Cursor and OpenCode token telemetry have different semantics; subscription costs are not directly comparable.",
    "The workload favors parallel delegation, so it does not estimate performance on coupled tasks.",
    "One Terra run transiently edited and restored a public test; one Luna run resumed a capped worker. Intention-to-treat and clean-block sensitivity results are both reported.",
    "The natural-Luna timeout is right-censored; comparisons using its capped duration are lower-bound speed advantages for the competing arm.",
    "Process isolation was policy-based rather than OS-enforced. Streams contain no hidden grader paths, but absence of access cannot be proven.",
    "Manifest, prompt, current fixture, and stored-score integrity are checked at analysis time; source files were not externally immutable before outcomes."
  ]
}
